The attached image is Figure 1, illustrating that Nano-11, a dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle, significantly enhances antigen-specific IgG titers similar to or greater than aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant. The box plots show anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone or co-administered with AH or Nano-11 at various doses (200, 50, and 12.5 µg). Nano-11 consistently induces a robust antibody response, even at a lower dose of 12.5 µg, demonstrating its potent immunopotentiating effect for prophylactic vaccines.